A CAF channel layout chunk that uses channel descriptions but lists none replaces the channels from
the audio description with an empty set. The AAC (without a magic cookie) and ADPCM decoders
accepted that, and AudioBuffer::new divided by the channel count of zero. The PCM decoder already
rejects zero channels the same way.

diff --git a/symphonia-codec-aac/src/aac/mod.rs b/symphonia-codec-aac/src/aac/mod.rs
index f005179..d686bc5 100644
--- a/symphonia-codec-aac/src/aac/mod.rs
+++ b/symphonia-codec-aac/src/aac/mod.rs
@@ -87,6 +87,11 @@ impl AacDecoder {
             _ => return unsupported_error("aac: channels or channel layout is required"),
         };
 
+        // At least one channel is required.
+        if channels.count() == 0 {
+            return unsupported_error("aac: number of channels cannot be 0");
+        }
+
         // Check complexity.
         if asc.object_type != AudioObjectType::Lc
             || asc.sbr_present
